        "original_id": "bcecb398-ae41-5f09-b56e-c7490a1c2e6c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Jungle Book (1967 film), The Lone Ranger (2013 film)\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- People: Mowgli, Bagheera, Baloo, Shere Khan, Gore Verbinski, Justin Haythe, Ted Elliott, Terry Rossio, Johnny Depp, Armie Hammer, William Fichtner, Barry Pepper, Ruth Wilson, James Badge Dale, Tom Wilkinson, Helena Bonham Carter, Tonto, John Reid\n- Concepts: radio series, American Old West\n\nFacts:\n- The Jungle Book is a 1967 American animated musical adventure film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- The Jungle Book follows Mowgli, a feral child raised in the Indian jungle by wolves, as Bagheera the panther and Baloo the bear try to persuade him to leave before Shere Khan arrives.\n- The Lone Ranger is a 2013 American western action film directed by Gore Verbinski and written by Justin Haythe, Ted Elliott, and Terry Rossio.\n- The Lone Ranger is based on the radio series of the same name and stars Johnny Depp as Tonto, the narrator, and Armie Hammer as John Reid, the Lone Ranger.\n- The Lone Ranger tells Tonto's memories of the duo's earliest efforts to fight local villainy and bring justice to the American Old West.\n- The Lone Ranger features William Fichtner, Barry Pepper, Ruth Wilson, James Badge Dale, Tom Wilkinson, and Helena Bonham Carter in supporting roles.\n- The Lone Ranger is the first theatrical film to feature the Lone Ranger and Tonto characters in more than 32 years.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
